00:00:00,010 --> 00:01:33,930
[ Watch on kissFlix.co ]

1
00:01:46,320 --> 00:01:48,560
Hello, is order 0354 ready?

2
00:01:48,560 --> 00:01:49,866
Let me check.

3
00:01:50,737 --> 00:01:52,692
Please hurry.

4
00:01:56,200 --> 00:01:58,201
<i>- In modern society,</i>
- Xuan.

5
00:01:58,201 --> 00:02:03,640
<i>more and more women are daring to
pursue what they love and aspire to.</i>

6
00:02:03,640 --> 00:02:08,720
<i>Their dreams rarely get held back
by their gender.</i>

7
00:02:08,720 --> 00:02:13,259
<i>Their careers take on diverse colors
precisely because of who they are.</i>

8
00:02:14,360 --> 00:02:18,905
<i>They are increasingly realizing that
instead of waiting for a hero to come,</i>

9
00:02:18,905 --> 00:02:23,245
<i>it's better to become their own trailblazers.</i>

10
00:02:24,040 --> 00:02:28,341
<i>Through their own efforts,
they earn social recognition and respect.</i>

11
00:02:29,105 --> 00:02:30,281
Thank you, ma'am.

12
00:02:30,281 --> 00:02:33,479
<i>- Would you trust a female driver?</i>
- Bye. Take care.

13
00:02:33,479 --> 00:02:36,650
<i>Would you trust a female doctor?</i>

14
00:02:37,869 --> 00:02:42,930
<i>Would you trust a female pilot's flying skills?</i>

15
00:02:50,600 --> 00:02:53,600
[Episode 17]
[Go Fly, Girl!]

16
00:03:15,760 --> 00:03:17,986
Si Xian, listen.

17
00:03:17,986 --> 00:03:20,966
First, this is absolutely not
what you saw online.

18
00:03:20,966 --> 00:03:24,320
Second, our PR Department is ready.
We'll issue a statement today.

19
00:03:24,320 --> 00:03:27,185
This isn't just for you,
but also for Hengshi Air's image.

20
00:03:27,185 --> 00:03:30,370
So we'll handle this matter
with the utmost seriousness.

21
00:03:30,370 --> 00:03:34,555
Most importantly, Mr. Fu is very angry.

22
00:03:34,555 --> 00:03:36,781
He was so restless
that he didn't sleep yesterday.

23
00:03:36,781 --> 00:03:38,600
He's worried you'll misunderstand.

24
00:03:38,600 --> 00:03:40,145
So he is already handling it.

25
00:03:40,145 --> 00:03:41,513
Are you finished?

26
00:03:42,177 --> 00:03:45,106
If yes, let him talk to me in person.

27
00:03:45,106 --> 00:03:48,451
Si Xian, can you promise me you'll talk calmly?

28
00:03:48,451 --> 00:03:51,483
Please don't fight, okay?

29
00:03:59,298 --> 00:04:02,719
Look at the timing.
We happened to run into a patrol.

30
00:04:02,719 --> 00:04:04,588
Alright, that's enough. Get back to work.

31
00:04:04,588 --> 00:04:06,640
- What?
- Just go.

32
00:04:06,640 --> 00:04:08,681
Go on, get busy. Hurry.

33
00:04:12,240 --> 00:04:15,440
Well, Mr. Fu is already in his office.

34
00:04:15,440 --> 00:04:19,305
He didn't sleep last night.
He's been waiting for you since early morning.

35
00:04:19,305 --> 00:04:21,163
Please, talk nicely.

36
00:04:24,520 --> 00:04:27,907
Didn't you say you wanted to talk? Go ahead.

37
00:04:30,354 --> 00:04:32,204
Let me, Si Xian.

38
00:04:39,200 --> 00:04:40,557
Please.

39
00:04:55,091 --> 00:04:56,581
Then I'll start.

40
00:04:58,160 --> 00:05:01,698
Li Zhi Huai and I are just friends.

41
00:05:03,170 --> 00:05:04,275
Go on.

42
00:05:04,275 --> 00:05:06,261
Her father was my high school teacher.

43
00:05:06,261 --> 00:05:08,560
We ran into each other in Chun City.

44
00:05:08,560 --> 00:05:10,785
Then we returned to Jiang City together.

45
00:05:10,785 --> 00:05:14,920
Later, her father found out
and insisted I go to his home for a drink.

46
00:05:14,920 --> 00:05:17,600
He's my teacher. I couldn't refuse.

47
00:05:17,600 --> 00:05:20,560
On the day you drank too much
and made me wait until late?

48
00:05:20,560 --> 00:05:23,800
Yes. But I wasn't drunk that day.

49
00:05:23,800 --> 00:05:26,720
I was just exhausted from busy work back then.

50
00:05:26,720 --> 00:05:28,930
You really won't admit it.

51
00:05:29,800 --> 00:05:32,680
- What about the flowers?
- The flowers...

52
00:05:32,680 --> 00:05:36,265
It was my teacher's birthday. I didn't go.

53
00:05:36,265 --> 00:05:40,080
So I asked Bai Yang to order some flowers.
The florist delivered them.

54
00:05:40,080 --> 00:05:42,825
That's right. Si Xian, I can vouch for him.

55
00:05:42,825 --> 00:05:46,377
Here are the payment records and the invoice.

56
00:05:48,840 --> 00:05:50,580
[Li Zhi Huai's Manager]

57
00:05:50,580 --> 00:05:52,040
This is bad.

58
00:05:52,730 --> 00:05:54,508
Her manager is calling.

59
00:05:59,746 --> 00:06:01,266
Answer it.

60
00:06:03,640 --> 00:06:06,426
<i>Hello? Bai Yang, this is Ying.</i>

61
00:06:06,426 --> 00:06:08,280
<i>I'm looking for Mr. Fu.</i>

62
00:06:08,280 --> 00:06:10,705
<i>Could you please put me through to him?</i>

63
00:06:10,705 --> 00:06:12,000
I'm here.

64
00:06:12,000 --> 00:06:13,425
<i>Hello, Mr. Fu.</i>

65
00:06:13,425 --> 00:06:17,510
I'm Zhi Huai's manager, Zhang Ying.
We've met before.

66
00:06:17,510 --> 00:06:19,000
<i>I'm truly sorry.</i>

67
00:06:19,000 --> 00:06:24,174
<i>I was overwhelmed yesterday,
so I only found the time to call you today.</i>

68
00:06:24,174 --> 00:06:28,079
<i>I sincerely apologize for yesterday's news.</i>

69
00:06:28,079 --> 00:06:31,545
<i>I didn't expect it to be exposed after so long.</i>

70
00:06:31,545 --> 00:06:34,169
<i>We're trying to suppress the buzz.</i>

71
00:06:34,169 --> 00:06:38,035
<i>But as you can see,
Zhi Huai is so popular right now.</i>

72
00:06:38,035 --> 00:06:40,774
<i>- We can't keep it down.</i>
- Get to the point.

73
00:06:41,480 --> 00:06:45,720
<i>Well, we'll keep looking for ways.
We'll issue a statement today.</i>

74
00:06:45,720 --> 00:06:49,560
<i>Is there anything on your end that
needs to be addressed?</i>

75
00:06:49,560 --> 00:06:51,380
Contact our PR Department.

76
00:06:56,108 --> 00:06:58,068
[Li Zhi Huai]

77
00:07:04,120 --> 00:07:05,516
Oh.

78
00:07:06,280 --> 00:07:08,160
This is getting complicated.

79
00:07:15,680 --> 00:07:17,439
[Speaker]

80
00:07:17,439 --> 00:07:19,279
<i>Hello, Ming Yu.</i>

81
00:07:19,279 --> 00:07:23,160
<i>My manager must have called you by now.</i>

82
00:07:23,160 --> 00:07:24,720
<i>I'm really sorry.</i>

83
00:07:24,720 --> 00:07:28,200
I didn't expect it
to cause you so much trouble.

84
00:07:28,200 --> 00:07:30,319
We're already handling it on our end.

85
00:07:30,319 --> 00:07:31,840
<i>I'm truly sorry.</i>

86
00:07:31,840 --> 00:07:34,505
It's already with our PR Department.

87
00:07:34,505 --> 00:07:39,249
<i>I know, but I still feel quite bad about it.</i>

88
00:07:39,249 --> 00:07:40,394
<i>How about this?</i>

89
00:07:40,394 --> 00:07:44,800
<i>When I return to Jiang City in a few days,
I'll treat you to a meal as an apology.</i>

90
00:07:44,800 --> 00:07:48,200
No need. We don't want any more trouble.

91
00:07:48,200 --> 00:07:51,025
About what I mentioned the other day...

92
00:07:51,025 --> 00:07:55,400
Contact our Marketing Department.
I've already been in touch with Time Pictures.

93
00:07:55,400 --> 00:07:59,985
I only care about the result.
I won't get involved in the details.

94
00:08:01,490 --> 00:08:03,036
Are you busy?

95
00:08:03,036 --> 00:08:06,520
Yes. I'm with my girlfriend.

96
00:08:07,640 --> 00:08:09,717
<i>Then I'll leave you to it.</i>

97
00:08:15,577 --> 00:08:17,939
It's an aviation-themed movie.

98
00:08:17,939 --> 00:08:20,360
Li Zhi Huai might be the female lead.

99
00:08:20,360 --> 00:08:23,546
The producers reached out to us,
seeking a collaboration.

100
00:08:23,546 --> 00:08:26,328
- That's all?
- That's all.

101
00:08:29,956 --> 00:08:32,356
Alright. I understand.

102
00:08:34,804 --> 00:08:37,187
But if such a thing happens again,

103
00:08:37,187 --> 00:08:40,767
just go to my father's grave
and explain it to him.

104
00:08:41,352 --> 00:08:42,539
Understood.

105
00:08:42,539 --> 00:08:43,880
Also, my dad loved to drink.

106
00:08:43,880 --> 00:08:46,080
- Si Xian.
- Remember to bring some alcohol.

107
00:08:49,891 --> 00:08:54,204
Mr. Fu, she wants you to drink with her father.

108
00:08:54,204 --> 00:08:55,724
I heard her.

109
00:08:56,440 --> 00:08:57,996
You're coming too.

110
00:09:25,000 --> 00:09:28,000
Ruan Si Xian. Good job.

111
00:09:28,000 --> 00:09:31,840
You didn't just barge into his office
and give him a piece of your mind.

112
00:09:31,840 --> 00:09:35,345
You could say you were mature and steady.

113
00:09:35,345 --> 00:09:37,618
Your acting was great, too.

114
00:09:38,843 --> 00:09:41,213
I bet you intimidated him.

115
00:09:42,705 --> 00:09:44,831
Look at him.

116
00:09:44,831 --> 00:09:48,556
Even if he had twice the guts,
he wouldn't dare do it again.

117
00:09:57,600 --> 00:10:00,440
<i>He's my old classmate.
He took time out to visit my father.</i>

118
00:10:00,440 --> 00:10:02,866
<i>We've been friends
for over a decade. Nothing more.</i>

119
00:10:02,866 --> 00:10:05,517
<i>If there's good news, I'll let you know.</i>

120
00:10:07,880 --> 00:10:10,858
[Si Xiao Zhen]
<i>What do you think about this Weibo post?</i>

121
00:10:11,800 --> 00:10:13,800
[Bian Xuan]<i>Same question.</i>

122
00:10:13,800 --> 00:10:16,120
<i>Wait. What does "took time out to visit" imply?</i>

123
00:10:16,120 --> 00:10:18,425
<i>How is that any different
from "visit specifically"?</i>

124
00:10:18,425 --> 00:10:21,640
<i>Why didn't she mention that
her dad was Fu Ming Yu's teacher?</i>

125
00:10:21,640 --> 00:10:26,391
<i>Classmates are classmates.
Why emphasize being friends for years?</i>

126
00:10:26,391 --> 00:10:28,081
<i>Exactly.</i>

127
00:10:32,624 --> 00:10:35,765
Even Fu Ming Yu has a day like this.

128
00:10:36,362 --> 00:10:38,027
What are you laughing at now?

129
00:10:38,027 --> 00:10:40,653
Fu Ming Yu's rumored girlfriend
issued a statement.

130
00:10:41,252 --> 00:10:42,889
Let me see.

131
00:10:48,655 --> 00:10:51,800
This statement... doesn't feel quite right.

132
00:10:51,800 --> 00:10:56,320
I bet she got the cold shoulder
from Fu Ming Yu and is saving face online.

133
00:10:56,320 --> 00:11:02,240
Isn't it obviously leaving things open-ended
for endless speculation?

134
00:11:02,240 --> 00:11:04,320
That woman was like this back in school.

135
00:11:04,320 --> 00:11:07,687
She always made it seem that
everyone was into her.

136
00:11:07,687 --> 00:11:10,031
Back then, she did like Fu Ming Yu.

137
00:11:10,031 --> 00:11:12,256
But Fu Ming Yu didn't like her back.

138
00:11:13,043 --> 00:11:14,420
What about you?

139
00:11:17,939 --> 00:11:21,200
Even less so. I'd never like her.
I have sharp eyes.

140
00:11:21,200 --> 00:11:25,360
With one look, I can tell
if a person is good or bad.

141
00:11:25,360 --> 00:11:27,110
I stay far away from her.

142
00:11:28,120 --> 00:11:31,537
How could Fu Ming Yu let her post
such a statement?

143
00:11:32,600 --> 00:11:34,200
We didn't agree.

144
00:11:34,200 --> 00:11:36,840
The PR Department
would never have agreed to it.

145
00:11:36,840 --> 00:11:41,720
Our PR Department made our demands
very clear to them. Absolutely clear.

146
00:11:41,720 --> 00:11:44,945
First, they must clarify that
you were only high school classmates.

147
00:11:44,945 --> 00:11:48,880
Second, they must explain
why you met and what you did.

148
00:11:48,880 --> 00:11:51,880
Their studio did post as requested.

149
00:11:51,880 --> 00:11:55,425
But I didn't expect Li Zhi Huai
to post another version herself.

150
00:11:55,425 --> 00:11:59,635
Every explanation only made it worse.
Look how far it has escalated.

151
00:12:00,560 --> 00:12:03,826
Tell the PR Department to show no mercy.

152
00:12:03,826 --> 00:12:08,130
Before the end of the day, the buzz
can stay high, but the narrative must change.

153
00:12:08,130 --> 00:12:09,130
Yes, sir.

154
00:12:12,240 --> 00:12:13,920
You saw it too.

155
00:12:13,920 --> 00:12:17,624
- When she gets angry, it's serious.
- Indeed.

156
00:12:17,624 --> 00:12:19,529
Do you want to
drink with her father before his grave?

157
00:12:19,529 --> 00:12:21,275
I'm allergic to alcohol.

158
00:12:21,275 --> 00:12:24,658
Then hurry up and treat everyone to milk tea.

159
00:12:24,658 --> 00:12:28,796
This started because of me,
but someone has to fix it.

160
00:12:38,428 --> 00:12:39,925
[Ruan Si Xian]

161
00:12:41,040 --> 00:12:47,640
<i>Sorry. The subscriber
you dialed is powered off.</i>

162
00:12:48,760 --> 00:12:52,720
<i>Sorry. The subscriber
you dialed is powered off.</i>

163
00:13:11,843 --> 00:13:13,563
Ruan Si Xian.

164
00:13:17,630 --> 00:13:19,318
Ruan Si Xian.

165
00:13:29,482 --> 00:13:36,082
<i>Sorry. The subscriber
you dialed is powered off.</i>

166
00:13:42,960 --> 00:13:45,426
Why are there still so many bad comments?

167
00:13:45,426 --> 00:13:48,720
Ms. Zhou, what did you do this afternoon?
What am I paying you for?

168
00:13:48,720 --> 00:13:51,105
What's the point of yelling at her?

169
00:13:51,105 --> 00:13:55,347
I told you not to post anything on your own.
Just stick to the studio's official line.

170
00:13:55,347 --> 00:13:58,064
Why won't you listen?

171
00:13:59,730 --> 00:14:02,440
And let me ask you. What was the rush?

172
00:14:02,440 --> 00:14:05,665
We've pretty much locked in
that female pilot project.

173
00:14:05,665 --> 00:14:08,640
All you need to do is
to play your role when the time comes.

174
00:14:08,640 --> 00:14:13,625
Besides, before you pull stunts like this,
could you at least give us a heads-up?

175
00:14:13,625 --> 00:14:16,019
You put us in a very difficult position.

176
00:14:16,846 --> 00:14:19,923
Rising stars are usually terrified
of dating rumors.

177
00:14:19,923 --> 00:14:23,706
But look at you.
You couldn't wait for the whole world to know.

178
00:14:23,706 --> 00:14:27,931
At least pick someone easy.
Yet you found such a tricky one.

179
00:14:28,520 --> 00:14:31,840
How was I supposed to know
he already had a girlfriend?

180
00:14:31,840 --> 00:14:35,105
Even if he didn't,
you still shouldn't have done this.

181
00:14:35,105 --> 00:14:38,105
What do you think we are? Some amateur troupe?

182
00:14:41,339 --> 00:14:45,197
In a moment, hand over
your social media accounts to Ms. Zhou.

183
00:14:49,160 --> 00:14:52,864
Ying, I'm sorry. I know I was wrong.

184
00:14:52,864 --> 00:14:55,800
I really wanted to get that role.

185
00:14:55,800 --> 00:14:57,360
Ying.

186
00:14:57,360 --> 00:15:01,226
Zhi Huai, the company is in a tough spot now.

187
00:15:01,226 --> 00:15:03,239
We'll see about the project.

188
00:15:09,370 --> 00:15:10,935
Ruan Si Xian.

189
00:15:12,757 --> 00:15:16,438
Ruan Si Xian. I can explain everything to you.

190
00:15:17,358 --> 00:15:21,272
I know you're in there.
Can you open the door first?

191
00:15:35,760 --> 00:15:38,000
What should I do?

192
00:16:13,520 --> 00:16:16,320
- Why are you here?
- You finally opened the door.

193
00:16:18,514 --> 00:16:20,419
Were you crying?

194
00:16:21,520 --> 00:16:24,023
Who's crying?

195
00:16:24,023 --> 00:16:26,928
You don't think
I was hiding in here crying, do you?

196
00:16:26,928 --> 00:16:30,073
Then why did you lock yourself
in your room all afternoon?

197
00:16:30,073 --> 00:16:32,618
I was studying.
There are so many exams every year.

198
00:16:32,618 --> 00:16:34,907
Don't I need time to prepare?

199
00:16:46,088 --> 00:16:47,808
- Really?
- What else?

200
00:16:47,808 --> 00:16:50,077
What do you think? Are you crazy?

201
00:16:51,187 --> 00:16:53,098
You really frightened me.

202
00:16:53,757 --> 00:16:55,742
Did you read Li Zhi Huai's statement?

203
00:16:55,742 --> 00:16:57,964
I read it on my way home.

204
00:16:57,964 --> 00:17:01,347
That classmate of yours is quite interesting.

205
00:17:01,347 --> 00:17:03,530
What about the latest one?

206
00:17:03,530 --> 00:17:05,633
The latest one?

207
00:17:05,633 --> 00:17:10,560
Regarding the recent online rumors
concerning our vice president, Mr. Fu Ming Yu,

208
00:17:10,560 --> 00:17:12,800
we make the following statement.

209
00:17:12,800 --> 00:17:17,825
First, Mr. Fu Ming Yu visited
Ms. Li's father late last autumn

210
00:17:17,825 --> 00:17:21,290
because he was Mr. Fu's
high school homeroom teacher.

211
00:17:21,290 --> 00:17:26,339
Expressing gratitude to one's teachers
is a virtue we all should uphold.

212
00:17:26,339 --> 00:17:30,923
Second, Mr. Fu and Ms. Li
have been busy with their own lives

213
00:17:30,923 --> 00:17:32,668
since graduating from high school.

214
00:17:32,668 --> 00:17:36,320
They have met only three times,
totaling two hours and five minutes.

215
00:17:36,320 --> 00:17:40,385
Two of those hours were spent
at a small gathering with teachers last year.

216
00:17:40,385 --> 00:17:43,011
While being classmates is fate,
that fate ends at graduation.

217
00:17:43,011 --> 00:17:45,160
Whether paths cross again
is a matter of chance.

218
00:17:45,160 --> 00:17:47,945
We hope everyone cherishes
their school-day friendships.

219
00:17:47,945 --> 00:17:51,760
Third, Vice President Fu is not single.

220
00:17:51,760 --> 00:17:53,760
He is in a stable relationship.

221
00:17:53,760 --> 00:17:57,400
Finally, visit Hengshi Air's official website
to register as a member.

222
00:17:57,400 --> 00:18:00,425
Our new spring routes are launching soon.

223
00:18:00,425 --> 00:18:03,970
Enjoy your exclusive flight butler service.

224
00:18:03,970 --> 00:18:06,732
Discover the world's best journeys
with Hengshi Air.

225
00:18:06,732 --> 00:18:10,344
That is so good.
Exhausting to read in the best way.

226
00:18:11,000 --> 00:18:13,920
I have to say, the PR Department
was fast this time.

227
00:18:13,920 --> 00:18:18,225
This statement is basically screaming
two words: Back off.

228
00:18:18,225 --> 00:18:20,291
They even threw in an ad at the end.

229
00:18:20,291 --> 00:18:22,556
As expected of a team trained by Fu Ming Yu.

230
00:18:22,556 --> 00:18:24,662
So, what are the comments saying now?

231
00:18:25,280 --> 00:18:26,800
Mostly mockery.

232
00:18:26,800 --> 00:18:30,320
Things like, "The tables turned so fast."

233
00:18:30,320 --> 00:18:32,224
Why did she even bother?

234
00:18:32,224 --> 00:18:35,409
It's all for work. For survival, I guess.

235
00:18:35,409 --> 00:18:38,280
Everyone has their own ways of doing things.

236
00:18:38,280 --> 00:18:42,983
- It's just that she chose the dumbest way.
- Right!

237
00:18:46,800 --> 00:18:49,060
I wonder how Si Xian is doing.

238
00:19:03,186 --> 00:19:05,960
What are you laughing at?
How can you still laugh?

239
00:19:05,960 --> 00:19:08,160
Come on, you're wasting public resources.

240
00:19:08,160 --> 00:19:10,000
I'm laughing at myself.

241
00:19:10,000 --> 00:19:13,160
I spent the whole afternoon
worrying about you for nothing.

242
00:19:13,160 --> 00:19:15,665
Indeed. You're a pilot.

243
00:19:15,665 --> 00:19:19,331
You wouldn't let
such a trivial matter get to you.

244
00:19:19,331 --> 00:19:22,573
Wrong. I'm actually a petty person.

245
00:19:23,160 --> 00:19:25,760
But she's just your high school classmate.

246
00:19:25,760 --> 00:19:27,480
Not even an ex.

247
00:19:27,480 --> 00:19:30,465
I'd rather spend time studying than gossiping.

248
00:19:30,465 --> 00:19:32,200
Weirdos don't come around every day,

249
00:19:32,200 --> 00:19:35,640
but professional exams
happen several times a year.

250
00:19:35,640 --> 00:19:36,440
Not mad anymore?

251
00:19:36,440 --> 00:19:39,880
Do I look like I have unlimited anger to spare?

252
00:19:39,880 --> 00:19:45,164
Who was it that
stormed into my office this morning?

253
00:19:45,164 --> 00:19:47,147
I can't be bothered to be mad at her.

254
00:19:47,836 --> 00:19:48,920
But you caused this.

255
00:19:48,920 --> 00:19:53,225
I'm mad at you for coming home that night
without telling me what happened.

256
00:19:53,225 --> 00:19:56,985
You didn't come clean immediately
when it happened.

257
00:19:57,697 --> 00:19:58,937
I'm sorry.

258
00:19:59,749 --> 00:20:01,734
It was my fault.

259
00:20:01,734 --> 00:20:03,335
It won't happen again.

260
00:20:04,178 --> 00:20:06,003
Don't be mad.

261
00:20:06,003 --> 00:20:07,680
But...

262
00:20:07,680 --> 00:20:09,985
is it that you don't trust me,

263
00:20:09,985 --> 00:20:11,680
or that you're worried about me?

264
00:20:11,680 --> 00:20:13,745
Which of us is more worried here?

265
00:20:13,745 --> 00:20:17,050
Anyway, you stood outside my door
all afternoon as punishment.

266
00:20:17,050 --> 00:20:19,873
Yet you're still sitting so close to me.

267
00:20:19,873 --> 00:20:22,938
- Wait. Then I have to protest.
- What are you protesting?

268
00:20:22,938 --> 00:20:25,984
- You caused this mess. How dare you protest?
- Of course I do.

269
00:20:25,984 --> 00:20:28,529
Lately, you keep ghosting me.

270
00:20:28,529 --> 00:20:31,473
Didn't we agree?
As soon as you land, you'd let me know.

271
00:20:31,473 --> 00:20:35,218
But look at you. Every time you land,
telling me is never the first thing you do.

272
00:20:35,218 --> 00:20:37,043
And now, you didn't even tell me you were back.

273
00:20:37,043 --> 00:20:38,840
I've been waiting for you all afternoon.

274
00:20:38,840 --> 00:20:41,937
I couldn't find you. You didn't
answer my calls or reply to my texts.

275
00:20:41,937 --> 00:20:45,547
Ruan Si Xian, I'm talking to you.
Do you have any idea how worried I was?

276
00:20:45,547 --> 00:20:47,800
What are you looking for?

277
00:20:47,800 --> 00:20:49,942
I'm looking for a way out.

278
00:20:49,942 --> 00:20:51,275
A way out?

279
00:20:52,200 --> 00:20:54,033
There's no way out of this.

280
00:20:56,200 --> 00:20:59,145
- Put me down.
- No. I have to find one too.

281
00:20:59,145 --> 00:21:00,784
I'm dizzy.

282
00:21:02,240 --> 00:21:05,527
A pilot getting dizzy? Is that your way out?

283
00:21:07,876 --> 00:21:09,262
I'm hungry.

284
00:21:09,262 --> 00:21:12,206
I want clam noodles.
I've been craving them for so long.

285
00:21:12,206 --> 00:21:15,537
You've got a total eye-candy right here.
You're not craving me?

286
00:21:15,537 --> 00:21:18,224
All you think about is clam noodles.

287
00:21:18,224 --> 00:21:19,440
I don't want to.

288
00:21:19,440 --> 00:21:21,680
You're going into clingy mode again.

289
00:21:21,680 --> 00:21:25,188
You're starting to disturb my normal life.

290
00:21:25,826 --> 00:21:29,400
Fine, fine.
I'm disturbing your normal life, "Captain."

291
00:21:29,400 --> 00:21:30,760
Then I'll leave, okay?

292
00:21:30,760 --> 00:21:33,619
You have to put me down first.

293
00:21:35,851 --> 00:21:37,375
Here's your way out.

294
00:21:38,155 --> 00:21:40,181
I'm leaving then.

295
00:21:40,181 --> 00:21:42,164
Who said you could leave?

296
00:21:42,164 --> 00:21:43,400
Didn't you tell me to leave?

297
00:21:43,400 --> 00:21:45,400
You leave just because I said so?

298
00:21:48,280 --> 00:21:51,680
See you at the clam noodle place.
Last one there pays the bill.

299
00:21:55,080 --> 00:21:56,866
She kissed me.

300
00:21:59,332 --> 00:22:01,617
As if you'd ever be late.

301
00:22:06,970 --> 00:22:10,347
Mr. Fu, the Catering Department's
new seasonal menu is ready.

302
00:22:10,347 --> 00:22:13,645
They've upgraded
the passengers' special ordering system.

303
00:22:13,645 --> 00:22:16,991
The tasting is currently scheduled
for this Friday at noon.

304
00:22:16,991 --> 00:22:19,680
Aren't we meeting the film company this Friday?

305
00:22:19,680 --> 00:22:22,200
Are we still going to work with them?

306
00:22:22,200 --> 00:22:24,560
The Brand Promotion Department
has suspended the contract.

307
00:22:24,560 --> 00:22:26,785
Did I say I wanted to terminate the deal?

308
00:22:26,785 --> 00:22:30,372
But things with Li Zhi Huai got pretty messy.

309
00:22:30,372 --> 00:22:32,038
Why not invest in such a good project?

310
00:22:32,038 --> 00:22:34,740
It's not like she's the only actress available.

311
00:22:34,740 --> 00:22:36,440
Stop sneaking bites.

312
00:22:36,440 --> 00:22:38,192
Name an actress you like.

313
00:22:38,192 --> 00:22:39,449
Cheng Yi Ke.

314
00:22:40,240 --> 00:22:43,984
Perfect. We can discuss the casting
when we have dinner with the producers.

315
00:22:43,984 --> 00:22:47,249
Also, have the Promotion Department
stay in touch with them.

316
00:22:47,249 --> 00:22:48,753
Sure. Leave it to us.

317
00:22:49,768 --> 00:22:52,354
- Looking forward to it.
- Everyone, watch your step.

318
00:22:52,354 --> 00:22:54,720
- Be careful.
- This way, sir.

319
00:22:54,720 --> 00:22:56,160
Please watch your step.

320
00:22:56,160 --> 00:22:59,200
Please show your boarding pass.
Watch your step.

321
00:22:59,200 --> 00:23:00,839
Watch your step. Stay safe.

322
00:23:00,839 --> 00:23:03,240
Please watch your step, everyone. Be careful.

323
00:23:03,240 --> 00:23:05,799
Welcome aboard Hengshi Air.

324
00:23:05,799 --> 00:23:07,960
- Can you hold this for me?
- Sure, no problem.

325
00:23:07,960 --> 00:23:09,779
Please watch your step.

326
00:23:10,599 --> 00:23:13,819
Excuse me, sir. Please stop taking photos.
Please proceed with boarding.

327
00:23:33,418 --> 00:23:35,227
Your boarding pass, please.

328
00:23:39,402 --> 00:23:41,219
Your boarding pass, please.

329
00:23:54,440 --> 00:23:57,040
Welcome aboard. Please head inside.

330
00:23:58,650 --> 00:24:00,932
Welcome aboard. Please head inside.

331
00:24:12,489 --> 00:24:15,693
Excuse me, sir. How can I help you?

332
00:24:16,480 --> 00:24:20,591
If you feel unwell or need any assistance,
please let me know anytime.

333
00:24:32,168 --> 00:24:33,707
Check it again.

334
00:24:36,930 --> 00:24:38,696
Mentor, there's another one here.

335
00:24:39,920 --> 00:24:42,905
<i>Captain, we found coins
in the engine's bypass duct.</i>

336
00:24:42,905 --> 00:24:44,489
<i>We suspect a passenger threw them.</i>

337
00:24:46,835 --> 00:24:49,964
Threw coins? How many have you found so far?

338
00:24:49,964 --> 00:24:52,454
<i>Only two. I'm not sure if there are more.</i>

339
00:24:52,454 --> 00:24:55,560
What era are we living in?
Why is someone still doing this?

340
00:24:55,560 --> 00:24:58,585
<i>It's not the first time.
It happens every few years.</i>

341
00:24:58,585 --> 00:25:00,610
<i>It's a real headache. We've called the police.</i>

342
00:25:00,610 --> 00:25:02,253
Got it.

343
00:25:03,347 --> 00:25:04,837
We can't take off.

344
00:25:07,331 --> 00:25:09,596
When are we taking off? Look at the time!

345
00:25:09,596 --> 00:25:11,621
Sir, please be patient.

346
00:25:11,621 --> 00:25:13,726
We'll take off as soon as possible.
Please wait a moment.

347
00:25:13,726 --> 00:25:18,542
<i>Ladies and gentlemen,
we found two coins near the aircraft.</i>

348
00:25:18,542 --> 00:25:21,240
<i>If you've lost coins,
please speak to the crew immediately.</i>

349
00:25:21,240 --> 00:25:22,792
Thank you.

350
00:25:22,792 --> 00:25:25,056
No one is going to admit to that.

351
00:25:26,385 --> 00:25:28,326
- Call the police.
- Okay.

352
00:25:36,680 --> 00:25:39,826
I already admitted I threw them.

353
00:25:39,826 --> 00:25:42,331
So what if I did?
Can't you just pick them up?

354
00:25:42,331 --> 00:25:44,273
I'll do it for you.

355
00:25:44,273 --> 00:25:47,298
Wait. How many coins did you throw in total?

356
00:25:47,298 --> 00:25:49,444
Four. I only had four in my pocket.

357
00:25:49,444 --> 00:25:51,640
I was supposed to throw nine.

358
00:25:51,640 --> 00:25:54,465
Do you know the consequences
of throwing those coins?

359
00:25:54,465 --> 00:25:55,931
I don't care.

360
00:25:55,931 --> 00:25:58,396
Hengshi Air hired a female pilot to fool us.

361
00:25:58,396 --> 00:26:00,221
Have you thought about the consequences?

362
00:26:00,221 --> 00:26:02,721
I only threw a few coins
to pray for luck. So what?

363
00:26:03,520 --> 00:26:07,760
Officer, I'm officially filing a report.
Let's just follow the procedure.

364
00:26:07,760 --> 00:26:09,946
You don't have to call the police.

365
00:26:09,946 --> 00:26:11,880
- What did I even do?
- You didn't do much.

366
00:26:11,880 --> 00:26:14,704
You simply tossed some coins into the engine.

367
00:26:14,704 --> 00:26:16,120
It's actually easy to handle.

368
00:26:16,120 --> 00:26:18,560
Just pay damages.
A few tens of thousands of yuan.

369
00:26:18,560 --> 00:26:22,742
But if I have to remove the engine,
repair it, and then put it back,

370
00:26:22,742 --> 00:26:24,421
you'll owe over 100,000.

371
00:26:27,480 --> 00:26:30,589
And about that female pilot you mentioned,

372
00:26:30,589 --> 00:26:34,182
she is hired at a high salary by our airline.

373
00:26:34,182 --> 00:26:36,768
You're suspected of violating Article 116
of the Criminal Law:

374
00:26:36,768 --> 00:26:37,992
Sabotaging a means of transport.

375
00:26:37,992 --> 00:26:39,880
- Hello?
- We've now accepted this case.

376
00:26:39,880 --> 00:26:42,475
- Please cooperate with the investigation.
- Were all four found?

377
00:26:43,960 --> 00:26:45,985
They were in the engine, right?

378
00:26:45,985 --> 00:26:47,376
Okay. Got it.

379
00:26:50,276 --> 00:26:52,748
Officer, I'll leave the rest to you.

380
00:27:05,280 --> 00:27:06,480
How's the situation?

381
00:27:06,480 --> 00:27:09,345
Was he even through nine years
of compulsory education?

382
00:27:09,345 --> 00:27:11,696
If this plane had taken off,
it would've been a disaster.

383
00:27:11,696 --> 00:27:14,557
And he called it a prayer.
He almost killed everyone.

384
00:27:15,600 --> 00:27:17,266
And look at this plane--

385
00:27:17,266 --> 00:27:19,450
Sounds like you're quite heartbroken over it.

386
00:27:19,450 --> 00:27:22,195
Of course. How could I not be?

387
00:27:22,195 --> 00:27:25,258
Is it your plane? Why do you even care?

388
00:27:25,258 --> 00:27:28,680
You're the one who told us to
treat Hengshi Air like home. Now it's not mine?

389
00:27:28,680 --> 00:27:31,429
So, is Hengshi Air actually my home or not?

390
00:27:32,760 --> 00:27:36,886
As long as I am yours,
Hengshi Air will always be your home.

391
00:27:39,040 --> 00:27:41,120
- I'm off.
- Go ahead.

392
00:27:42,314 --> 00:27:44,499
- Stay safe.
- Okay.

393
00:27:58,626 --> 00:27:59,865
Here.

394
00:28:02,036 --> 00:28:05,230
If you ask me, don't bother.

395
00:28:05,993 --> 00:28:10,218
With a video like this, we'd better off
fake dating and film scripted couple stuff.

396
00:28:10,218 --> 00:28:11,564
That'd gain followers fast.

397
00:28:11,564 --> 00:28:13,149
Do I look like a masochist to you?

398
00:28:13,149 --> 00:28:17,493
If we fake being together,
your army of exes will hunt me down online.

399
00:28:17,493 --> 00:28:19,368
They'll get my account banned.

400
00:28:19,368 --> 00:28:22,353
But this video of yours has no highlights.

401
00:28:22,353 --> 00:28:24,098
Who would want to watch it?

402
00:28:24,098 --> 00:28:27,409
Then what highlights do you want?

403
00:28:28,618 --> 00:28:31,720
A video needs jokes, which you don't have.

404
00:28:31,720 --> 00:28:34,545
It needs long legs,
which you don't have either.

405
00:28:34,545 --> 00:28:37,489
All you're doing
is recording ordinary women at work.

406
00:28:37,489 --> 00:28:40,514
If it gets over 100 likes, I'll eat grapes
while doing a handstand.

407
00:28:40,514 --> 00:28:44,985
Say one more word, and I'll chop off
your legs and put them in this video.

408
00:28:44,985 --> 00:28:46,571
Even if no one watches it,

409
00:28:46,571 --> 00:28:50,048
I'm still going to make what I want
and express what I believe.

410
00:28:50,048 --> 00:28:53,858
Besides eating grapes, what else can you do?
All you do is criticize my video.

411
00:28:53,858 --> 00:28:55,440
Go away. I don't want to see you.

412
00:28:55,440 --> 00:28:58,465
- You're so annoying. Go away.
- No! I'll just watch you edit.

413
00:28:58,465 --> 00:29:01,436
I knew it.
When you need me, you sweet-talk to me.

414
00:29:01,436 --> 00:29:04,320
When you don't, you're ready to
chop off my legs and kick me out.

415
00:29:04,320 --> 00:29:07,559
Do you know what this is called?
The modern-day "Farmer and the Viper."

416
00:29:07,559 --> 00:29:09,200
"Mr. Dong Guo and the Wolf."

417
00:29:09,200 --> 00:29:11,845
"Zheng You An and Yan An."

418
00:29:13,360 --> 00:29:17,680
- No, you eat it. I can't eat anymore.
- Don't you love grapes?

419
00:29:24,532 --> 00:29:26,393
- Dad.
- Mr. Zheng.

420
00:29:27,604 --> 00:29:29,189
Yan An, you're here too.

421
00:29:29,189 --> 00:29:30,679
What a coincidence.

422
00:29:31,835 --> 00:29:34,540
What brings you all the way here?

423
00:29:34,540 --> 00:29:37,444
Since my studio opened,
you haven't cared or asked about it.

424
00:29:37,444 --> 00:29:39,240
Now you're here all of a sudden.

425
00:29:39,240 --> 00:29:42,838
What's going on?
Is the family business failing?

426
00:29:45,012 --> 00:29:47,037
So this is your studio.

427
00:29:47,037 --> 00:29:50,887
Can you stop making small talk?
What kind of question is that?

428
00:29:50,887 --> 00:29:53,776
I'm sitting right here.
If this isn't my studio, then what is it?

429
00:29:53,776 --> 00:29:58,720
Don't tell me that you're here
because you got lost and just wandered in.

430
00:29:58,720 --> 00:30:00,447
Is that how you talk to me?

431
00:30:00,447 --> 00:30:03,751
I'm talking to you the same way I always do.

432
00:30:13,748 --> 00:30:15,881
- Yan An.
- Mr. Zheng.

433
00:30:15,881 --> 00:30:18,578
Have you two been together all the time lately?

434
00:30:18,578 --> 00:30:20,323
Not all the time.

435
00:30:20,323 --> 00:30:23,548
In the evenings,
we still go our separate ways home.

436
00:30:23,548 --> 00:30:24,548
Right.

437
00:30:26,559 --> 00:30:28,960
- Sit down.
- Mr. Zheng, please sit.

438
00:30:28,960 --> 00:30:30,811
I said, you sit.

439
00:30:44,067 --> 00:30:45,566
Yan An.

440
00:30:46,630 --> 00:30:49,761
What exactly... is...

441
00:30:50,440 --> 00:30:51,904
your relationship?

442
00:30:51,904 --> 00:30:53,730
Dad!

443
00:30:53,730 --> 00:30:56,154
What exactly are you here for?
Conducting a census?

444
00:30:56,154 --> 00:30:57,900
I'm asking him.

445
00:30:57,900 --> 00:31:01,284
I say one sentence,
and you've got a hundred responses ready.

446
00:31:01,284 --> 00:31:04,213
You started it,
but you won't let me speak? You--

447
00:31:06,160 --> 00:31:08,680
Yan... Yan An. How's everything at home lately?

448
00:31:08,680 --> 00:31:10,720
Everything is fine.

449
00:31:10,720 --> 00:31:12,560
- Is your father well?
- He's doing fine.

450
00:31:12,560 --> 00:31:14,320
So is my mom.

451
00:31:16,000 --> 00:31:19,960
Since you're always here,
you haven't been helping at home, right?

452
00:31:19,960 --> 00:31:22,560
My family's business
doesn't need me to manage it.

453
00:31:22,560 --> 00:31:24,958
You're a grown man now, right?

454
00:31:24,958 --> 00:31:27,544
You should start taking care of
the family business.

455
00:31:27,544 --> 00:31:31,089
Your father and I will get old eventually.

456
00:31:31,089 --> 00:31:32,634
I understand.

457
00:31:32,634 --> 00:31:37,260
You know, You An is my only precious daughter.

458
00:31:37,260 --> 00:31:39,525
I'm not some feudal patriarch.

459
00:31:39,525 --> 00:31:42,669
If you two are dating, I won't object.

460
00:31:42,669 --> 00:31:46,440
But I have two requirements.
You must agree to them.

461
00:31:46,440 --> 00:31:48,520
Please, go ahead.

462
00:31:51,851 --> 00:31:56,196
First of all, I don't care about the past.

463
00:31:56,196 --> 00:32:01,560
But from now on, you have to tie up
all your loose ends with other women.

464
00:32:01,560 --> 00:32:02,973
Sure.

465
00:32:03,880 --> 00:32:07,720
Second, the Zheng family
has hit a rough patch lately,

466
00:32:07,720 --> 00:32:11,802
and we're facing a few setbacks,
but our family wealth is still intact.

467
00:32:11,802 --> 00:32:13,155
I hope...

468
00:32:14,080 --> 00:32:16,944
you can take charge in the future.

469
00:32:16,944 --> 00:32:18,774
I understand. No problem.

470
00:32:19,540 --> 00:32:22,200
What do you mean, "no problem"?
I have a problem.

471
00:32:22,200 --> 00:32:25,920
And you claim you're not a feudal patriarch.
Look at you. What kind of attitude is this?

472
00:32:25,920 --> 00:32:27,465
You're not like this at home.

473
00:32:27,465 --> 00:32:29,931
Why does he have to
take over my family business?

474
00:32:29,931 --> 00:32:33,320
Can't I handle it? Why do you
trust him so much? I get it now.

475
00:32:33,320 --> 00:32:36,545
You've been rushing me to get married
just because you're looking for an heir.

476
00:32:36,545 --> 00:32:39,250
You should just transfer
all your assets to him.

477
00:32:39,250 --> 00:32:41,119
Why take such a roundabout way?

478
00:32:41,119 --> 00:32:43,799
I'm your only daughter, yet you never let me
get involved in family matters.

479
00:32:43,799 --> 00:32:46,599
You'd rather trust him than me.
You don't trust me at all.

480
00:32:46,599 --> 00:32:48,777
And you call this spoiling me?

481
00:32:50,840 --> 00:32:53,440
I'm telling your mom.

482
00:32:53,440 --> 00:32:55,723
All you ever do is tell my mom.

483
00:32:57,200 --> 00:32:59,185
Why the hell slap a card down?
What's that supposed to mean?

484
00:32:59,185 --> 00:33:00,642
Take care, Mr. Zheng.

485
00:33:04,490 --> 00:33:07,980
I can't use the simulator without a booking.

486
00:33:08,915 --> 00:33:13,501
There are no movies I want to see,
and I don't want to go home.

487
00:33:13,501 --> 00:33:16,304
This time off is useless to me.

488
00:33:31,139 --> 00:33:33,120
Waiting for a car?

489
00:33:33,120 --> 00:33:35,480
No, I'm waiting for you.

490
00:33:35,480 --> 00:33:36,991
Waiting for me?

491
00:33:37,916 --> 00:33:39,700
Is something the matter?

492
00:33:40,716 --> 00:33:45,514
There's something... I'd like to ask you about.

493
00:33:46,560 --> 00:33:47,720
Go ahead.

494
00:33:47,720 --> 00:33:50,255
When you quit and went to the flight academy,

495
00:33:51,001 --> 00:33:53,030
it must have been a tough decision.

496
00:34:06,360 --> 00:34:09,520
I guess there are no permanent enemies.

497
00:34:09,520 --> 00:34:12,134
They can even sit and drink together.

498
00:34:13,073 --> 00:34:15,418
Isn't that how girls' friendships are?

499
00:34:15,418 --> 00:34:18,163
You break up and make up all the time.

500
00:34:18,163 --> 00:34:21,468
Ever since you were kids,
you'd be friends one day and fall out the next.

501
00:34:21,468 --> 00:34:23,680
Don't give me that "you girls" stuff.

502
00:34:23,680 --> 00:34:27,047
Don't you guys ever fall out and then make up?
Get to work!

503
00:34:27,720 --> 00:34:30,080
Anyway, I'm really sorry.

504
00:34:30,080 --> 00:34:35,625
Whether you forgive me or not,
I should apologize for what I did to you.

505
00:34:35,625 --> 00:34:37,691
I'm truly sorry.

506
00:34:37,691 --> 00:34:39,000
It's water under the bridge.

507
00:34:39,000 --> 00:34:43,880
Because those things didn't really hurt me.

508
00:34:43,880 --> 00:34:46,434
Still, I shouldn't have done them.

509
00:34:47,400 --> 00:34:50,706
I came to you despite the awkwardness

510
00:34:50,706 --> 00:34:54,996
because I don't know anyone else
with a similar experience.

511
00:34:55,850 --> 00:34:58,594
You want to quit and go to flight academy?

512
00:34:58,594 --> 00:35:01,159
Not to flight academy. I'm over the age limit.

513
00:35:02,107 --> 00:35:04,252
But I do want to resign.

514
00:35:04,252 --> 00:35:08,157
However, I haven't fully made up my mind yet.

515
00:35:08,157 --> 00:35:13,307
So I wanted to ask you,
why were you so resolute back then?

516
00:35:15,116 --> 00:35:19,420
Back then,
there was definitely some spite involved.

517
00:35:19,420 --> 00:35:21,503
I just gritted my teeth and went for it.

518
00:35:22,729 --> 00:35:25,459
Why do you suddenly want to quit?

519
00:35:27,395 --> 00:35:28,984
Maybe...

520
00:35:30,011 --> 00:35:32,673
I feel like I can't see a future here.

521
00:35:33,320 --> 00:35:36,544
It's like I've hit a dead end.

522
00:35:36,544 --> 00:35:38,440
You could transfer to another department.

523
00:35:38,440 --> 00:35:42,545
And at Hengshi Air,
there aren't many senior pursers like you.

524
00:35:42,545 --> 00:35:45,930
Maybe in a few years,
you'll be promoted to management.

525
00:35:45,930 --> 00:35:47,823
There's still hope.

526
00:35:49,720 --> 00:35:52,801
That sounds so familiar.

527
00:35:53,444 --> 00:35:55,230
But then again,

528
00:35:55,230 --> 00:35:59,344
being a flight attendant did bring me a lot.

529
00:36:00,574 --> 00:36:03,918
At least it helped me to
leave the home I grew up in.

530
00:36:03,918 --> 00:36:08,925
But you know what? The ironic thing is,
all my motivation in the past

531
00:36:08,925 --> 00:36:12,441
was to have a little home of my own.

532
00:36:12,441 --> 00:36:15,627
So I worked hard for a long time for that.

533
00:36:15,627 --> 00:36:18,942
I tolerated Yue Yang time and again.

534
00:36:19,971 --> 00:36:22,237
I even came after you to mark my territory.

535
00:36:22,237 --> 00:36:25,342
In the end, I found out that
he didn't like me at all.

536
00:36:25,342 --> 00:36:27,642
All the perfection was just in my head.

537
00:36:28,371 --> 00:36:30,916
I often thought, I am so great.

538
00:36:30,916 --> 00:36:36,248
Why doesn't Yue Yang like me?
How could he not like me?

539
00:36:40,502 --> 00:36:43,607
But after going through so much,

540
00:36:43,607 --> 00:36:46,280
I think I've grown a little.

541
00:36:46,280 --> 00:36:48,080
At least now...

542
00:36:49,716 --> 00:36:53,071
I can accept that someone may not like me.

543
00:36:54,480 --> 00:36:57,920
You know what? Sometimes I really envy you.

544
00:36:57,920 --> 00:37:03,025
To be honest, that envy
comes with a bit of resentment.

545
00:37:03,025 --> 00:37:05,280
Maybe that's just human nature.

546
00:37:05,280 --> 00:37:10,290
I often tell myself not to think that way.
But I just can't control myself.

547
00:37:10,290 --> 00:37:12,074
I'm so unwilling to accept it.

548
00:37:12,074 --> 00:37:16,832
Why do I work so hard
only to always be just a little bit behind?

549
00:37:18,112 --> 00:37:24,095
Ever since I was a kid, I've never been able to
get anything I truly wanted.

550
00:37:32,520 --> 00:37:35,920
Do you think I'm asking for too much?

551
00:37:35,920 --> 00:37:38,430
Is that why I'm so unhappy?

552
00:37:38,430 --> 00:37:40,471
What's wrong with having desires?

553
00:37:41,349 --> 00:37:43,520
You deserve them.

554
00:37:43,520 --> 00:37:46,865
And over these years,
you've worked harder than anyone.

555
00:37:46,865 --> 00:37:48,480
You're better than anyone.

556
00:37:48,480 --> 00:37:51,524
You just met someone who let you down.

557
00:37:53,188 --> 00:37:57,492
You can't let this setback
make you deny yourself.

558
00:37:57,492 --> 00:38:01,782
If you want someone
who won't let you down or betray you,

559
00:38:03,082 --> 00:38:04,738
that person can only be you.

560
00:38:17,634 --> 00:38:20,271
So it's not too late, right?

561
00:38:21,280 --> 00:38:23,613
You think I can still be saved, right?

562
00:38:34,749 --> 00:38:36,149
Get away from me!

563
00:38:36,149 --> 00:38:39,134
Why are you so angry?
Didn't you take that card?

564
00:38:39,134 --> 00:38:41,881
I told you, I'm not going to use it.
Don't follow me!

565
00:38:41,881 --> 00:38:44,520
Why are you so mad at me?
I didn't do anything to you.

566
00:38:44,520 --> 00:38:45,720
Yan An.

567
00:38:46,442 --> 00:38:48,987
We've been hanging out for so long,
flirting back and forth,

568
00:38:48,987 --> 00:38:50,932
but you've never confessed or made a promise.

569
00:38:50,932 --> 00:38:54,037
Then my dad showed up today,
and you just took over my family business.

570
00:38:54,037 --> 00:38:56,560
Nice way to reap the benefits.

571
00:38:56,560 --> 00:38:59,600
I didn't take it. Your dad forced it on me.

572
00:38:59,600 --> 00:39:00,838
Forced it?

573
00:39:02,546 --> 00:39:05,840
And you just took it?
You just took it because he offered?

574
00:39:05,840 --> 00:39:09,948
I panicked and took it.
I wouldn't actually keep it.

575
00:39:10,760 --> 00:39:12,722
If I gave myself to you, would you take me?

576
00:39:22,160 --> 00:39:25,201
We're best friends.
Why are you saying all this?

577
00:39:26,676 --> 00:39:28,409
Yan An.

578
00:39:28,409 --> 00:39:30,400
You're such a jerk.

579
00:39:30,400 --> 00:39:31,740
Don't follow me.

580
00:39:31,740 --> 00:39:34,880
Zheng You An, let me explain.
Don't run. There's a step there.

581
00:39:34,880 --> 00:39:36,592
- Seriously, don't run.
- Go away!

582
00:39:36,592 --> 00:39:38,440
Zheng You An!

583
00:39:38,440 --> 00:39:40,625
Xuan.

584
00:39:40,625 --> 00:39:42,880
Give me your strongest drink.

585
00:39:42,880 --> 00:39:45,866
Look who's here. The lightweight
who can't handle one Long Island.

586
00:39:45,866 --> 00:39:48,640
You're here early today. There they are.

587
00:39:50,160 --> 00:39:53,745
Si Xian.

588
00:39:53,745 --> 00:39:56,770
I've had a long day.

589
00:39:56,770 --> 00:39:58,600
What happened now?

590
00:39:58,600 --> 00:40:02,386
It's so good that you're here.
You have to stay with me tonight.

591
00:40:02,386 --> 00:40:03,970
We're drinking until we drop.

592
00:40:03,970 --> 00:40:06,040
I'm really full of grievances.

593
00:40:06,040 --> 00:40:08,000
- Only you understand me.
- Alright.

594
00:40:08,000 --> 00:40:09,440
Don't just wail. Tell me what happened.

595
00:40:09,440 --> 00:40:11,880
Let me have a drink first.

596
00:40:11,880 --> 00:40:16,066
- Xuan, drinks!
- Coming!

597
00:40:16,066 --> 00:40:18,880
Before you have strong liquor,
shouldn't you eat something first?

598
00:40:18,880 --> 00:40:20,404
Drinks coming right up.

599
00:40:23,474 --> 00:40:26,200
And this is...?

600
00:40:26,200 --> 00:40:30,280
She's a purser at our airline. Zi Yue.

601
00:40:31,226 --> 00:40:32,925
Zi Yue.

602
00:40:35,073 --> 00:40:36,618
You've been crying.

603
00:40:36,618 --> 00:40:38,884
It's nothing. I just got a little emotional.

604
00:40:38,884 --> 00:40:42,040
Who upset you? Tell me.
We'll chew them out tonight.

605
00:40:42,040 --> 00:40:44,226
You'll feel better once you let it out.

606
00:40:44,226 --> 00:40:45,989
There, there, don't cry.

607
00:40:47,280 --> 00:40:50,640
Give her a small serving.
Just a tiny bit will do.

608
00:40:50,640 --> 00:40:52,718
Any less and there'd be nothing left.

609
00:40:54,680 --> 00:40:57,248
- See what you'd like to drink.
- I'll just have water today.

610
00:40:57,248 --> 00:40:59,840
Who upset you? Tell me.
We'll chew them out tonight.

611
00:40:59,840 --> 00:41:02,780
- Who knows how drunk she'd be?
- Don't worry. I didn't give her much.

612
00:41:07,280 --> 00:41:10,402
Are you two together?

613
00:41:14,516 --> 00:41:17,814
What am I to her? Just a friend.

614
00:41:18,593 --> 00:41:20,738
At least you're self-aware.

615
00:41:30,400 --> 00:41:33,079
I'm so angry I could punch him.

616
00:41:33,079 --> 00:41:34,615
Why wasn't I on that flight?

617
00:41:34,615 --> 00:41:37,640
If I were there, I'd grab him by the collar
and slap him a few times.

618
00:41:37,640 --> 00:41:40,936
What? Threw coins?

619
00:41:40,936 --> 00:41:44,120
He just thinks women
can't do these things well, right?

620
00:41:44,120 --> 00:41:46,960
My dad is exactly like him.

621
00:41:46,960 --> 00:41:49,186
He doesn't trust me to run his hotels.

622
00:41:49,186 --> 00:41:52,236
He'd rather trust a complete outsider like him.
I don't even know why.

623
00:41:52,236 --> 00:41:55,760
Just because he's a man?
Who is he to my family, anyway?

624
00:41:55,760 --> 00:41:58,680
He and my dad aren't even related.

625
00:41:58,680 --> 00:42:02,278
- And between him and me, we're--
- Friends.

626
00:42:04,080 --> 00:42:05,831
That's what he just said.

627
00:42:07,480 --> 00:42:09,040
Yes.

628
00:42:09,040 --> 00:42:11,364
Friends!

629
00:42:12,520 --> 00:42:14,505
He doesn't even have the guts to woo me.

630
00:42:14,505 --> 00:42:16,381
He doesn't dare. What a real man!

631
00:42:16,381 --> 00:42:18,800
What does my dad see in him?
I really don't get it.

632
00:42:18,800 --> 00:42:20,700
He's so timid.

633
00:42:21,589 --> 00:42:23,403
Slow down.

634
00:42:25,880 --> 00:42:27,226
That's not right.

635
00:42:27,226 --> 00:42:29,169
What's wrong?

636
00:42:29,169 --> 00:42:31,433
I've drunk so much,

637
00:42:31,433 --> 00:42:33,699
but my mind is still so clear.

638
00:42:34,458 --> 00:42:35,840
Xuan.

639
00:42:35,840 --> 00:42:38,037
Why is your alcohol so weak? Is it fake?

640
00:42:38,037 --> 00:42:40,945
You can't say that.

641
00:42:40,945 --> 00:42:43,120
This is a reputable bar.

642
00:42:43,800 --> 00:42:45,473
- Yan An.
- Yes?

643
00:42:45,473 --> 00:42:47,320
Get me something strong.

644
00:42:47,320 --> 00:42:48,880
- Okay.
- Hurry up.

645
00:42:49,995 --> 00:42:51,875
- Something weak.
- Of course.

646
00:42:55,572 --> 00:42:59,076
- It doesn't taste like alcohol at all.
- Miss, do you need anything else?

647
00:42:59,076 --> 00:43:00,879
- Get lost.
- Understood.

648
00:43:02,261 --> 00:43:04,686
Alright. You guys enjoy yourselves.

649
00:43:04,686 --> 00:43:08,231
I have things to do tomorrow.
I'll head out first.

650
00:43:08,231 --> 00:43:11,015
Zi Yue, did I talk too much just now?

651
00:43:11,015 --> 00:43:13,840
No. But I actually enjoyed
listening to you talk.

652
00:43:13,840 --> 00:43:15,186
- Then I--
- Alright.

653
00:43:15,186 --> 00:43:17,240
She has a flight tomorrow. I'll see her out.

654
00:43:17,240 --> 00:43:18,607
Don't drink too much.

655
00:43:18,607 --> 00:43:20,480
Zi Yue.

656
00:43:20,480 --> 00:43:24,105
If anyone upsets you,
tell me. I'll chew them out!

657
00:43:24,105 --> 00:43:26,960
- If words don't work, I'll just hit them!
- Hey.

658
00:43:26,960 --> 00:43:29,425
What are you doing, my friend?

659
00:43:29,425 --> 00:43:31,168
What are you talking about?

